<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Sale Deed — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Transfer of Property Act 1882 (Sec 54), Registration Act 1908 (Sec 17), Karnataka Stamp Act 1957</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>5% Stamp Duty + 10% Cess + 2% Surcharge on Market/Guidance Value in Karnataka</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Compulsory Registration at Sub-Registrar Office under Section 17 Registration Act (2% Registration Fee)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Directly presented and executed before Sub-Registrar with two adult witnesses holding Aadhaar</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>Senior Civil Judge / District Court of the jurisdiction where immovable property is situated</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>3 years for cancellation of deed or recovery of possession under Limitation Act</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Registered Mother Deed / Previous Sale Deeds (30-year flow of title); Khata Certificate and Khata Extract (e-Khata / A-Khata from BBMP/Gram Panchayat); Latest Property Tax Paid Receipts and Encumbrance Certificate (EC - Form 15 for 30 years); Sanctioned Building Plan & Occupancy Certificate (if apartment/commercial building); PAN Card & Aadhaar Card of Vendor and Purchaser + TDS 194-IA 1% Challan</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">SALE DEED</div>
<div class="draft-body">DEED OF ABSOLUTE SALE OF IMMOVABLE PROPERTY

This DEED OF ABSOLUTE SALE is executed on this _____ day of _______________, 2026 at ________________________, Karnataka, by and between:

VENDOR:
Mr./Ms. __________________________________________________,
S/o, D/o, W/o ____________________________________________,
Aged about _____ years, PAN: ____________________________,
Aadhaar No.: ____________________________________________,
Residing at: ____________________________________________,
(Hereinafter called the "VENDOR", which expression shall include his/her heirs, legal representatives, successors, and assigns of the FIRST PART);

IN FAVOUR OF

PURCHASER:
Mr./Ms. __________________________________________________,
S/o, D/o, W/o ____________________________________________,
Aged about _____ years, PAN: ____________________________,
Aadhaar No.: ____________________________________________,
Residing at: ____________________________________________,
(Hereinafter called the "PURCHASER", which expression shall include his/her heirs, legal representatives, successors, and assigns of the SECOND PART).

WHEREAS the Vendor is the absolute and lawful owner in peaceful possession and enjoyment of all that piece and parcel of immovable residential property bearing Site/Flat No. __________, situated at ____________________________________________________, more fully described in the SCHEDULE hereunder (hereinafter referred to as the "SCHEDULE PROPERTY").

AND WHEREAS the Vendor acquired the Schedule Property by virtue of Registered Sale Deed dated ___/___/____ registered as Document No. ___________ in the office of the Sub-Registrar, ________________________.

AND WHEREAS the Vendor has marketable title, free from all encumbrances, attachments, liens, litigations, court injunctions, mortgages, or government acquisitions of any nature.

AND WHEREAS the Vendor has agreed to sell and the Purchaser has agreed to purchase the Schedule Property for a total agreed sale consideration of Rs. ____________/- (Rupees _________________________________________ only).

NOW THIS DEED OF SALE WITNESSETH AS FOLLOWS:

1. CONSIDERATION:
In pursuance of the agreement and in consideration of the total sum of Rs. ____________/- paid by the Purchaser to the Vendor in the following manner:
- Rs. ____________/- via Cheque/DD/NEFT No. ____________ dated ___/___/2026 drawn on ____________________ Bank;
- Rs. ____________/- via TDS deducted under Section 194-IA Income Tax Act (Challan Form 26QB No. ____________);
the Vendor hereby acknowledges receipt of the entire sale consideration in full satisfaction.

2. TRANSFER OF ABSOLUTE TITLE & POSSESSION:
The Vendor hereby grants, conveys, sells, transfers, and assigns unto the Purchaser, absolutely and forever, all rights, title, interest, claims, and easements of the Schedule Property. The Vendor has delivered vacant, physical, and peaceful possession of the Schedule Property to the Purchaser on this day.

3. FREEDOM FROM ENCUMBRANCES:
The Vendor covenants that the Schedule Property is free from all encumbrances, mortgages, charges, court attachments, lis pendens, tax arrears, or maintenance claims.

4. INDEMNITY:
If any defect in title, secret mortgage, or third-party claim is discovered, the Vendor shall indemnify and hold harmless the Purchaser from all losses, damages, costs, and expenses.

5. HANDING OVER OF DOCUMENTS:
The Vendor has handed over all original title deeds, Khata certificates, tax receipts, and Encumbrance Certificates to the Purchaser.

6. KHATA MUTATION:
The Purchaser is entitled to effect Khata transfer / mutation in their name before the competent municipal authority (BBMP / City Corporation) without further reference to the Vendor.

SCHEDULE OF THE PROPERTY:
All that residential property bearing No. ____________, situated at ________________________________________________, measuring East to West: _____ ft, North to South: _____ ft, total area: _____ sq. ft.
Bounded by:
EAST: _______________________________________
WEST: _______________________________________
NORTH: ______________________________________
SOUTH: ______________________________________

IN WITNESS WHEREOF the Vendor and Purchaser have executed this Sale Deed on the date first mentioned above.

VENDOR:                                         PURCHASER:
Signature: __________________________            Signature: __________________________
Name: _______________________________            Name: _______________________________

WITNESSES:
1. Signature: _______________________            2. Signature: _______________________
   Name: ____________________________               Name: ____________________________
   Address: _________________________               Address: _________________________
   Aadhaar: _________________________               Aadhaar: _________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
